<title>GREECE: ALPHA CREDIT CUTS PRIME RATE TO 15.5PCT.</title>
<headline>ALPHA CREDIT CUTS PRIME RATE TO 15.5PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Credit Bank said on Friday it will cut its prime lending rate by 125 basis points down to 15.5 percent, effective January 20.</p>
<p>The bank is also lowering its savings deposit rates by 75 basis points to 10.75 and 10.0 percent respectively for its Alpha 410 and Alpha 400 accounts.  </p>
<p>Alpha Credit's new deposit rate structure will have as</p>
<p>follows:</p>
<p>SAVINGS DEPOSIT RATES:</p>
<p>    Alpha 410	  10.75%</p>
<p>    Alpha 400	  10.00%</p>
<p>    Alpha 100	  11.75%  (amounts over 50 million drs)</p>
<p>    Alpha 500	  10.25%  (amounts over 50 million drs)</p>
<p>    TIME DEPOSIT RATES:     10.0%</p>
<p>REPOS (one week-12 months): negotiable</p>
<p>Alpha's new lending rates will be the following:</p>
<p>    Prime rate	 15.5%   (working capital, fixed assets)</p>
<p>    Alpha 500	  15.5%   (business)</p>
<p>    Alpha 620	  13.5%   (small business)</p>
<p>    Alpha 810	  11.5%   (nine-year business housing loan)</p>
<p>    Alpha 800	  11.5%   (15-year mortgage)</p>
<p>    Alpha 100	  19.0%</p>
<p>    Personal loans   22.0%</p>
<p>    Housing loan     15.75%  (floating rate loan)</p>
<p>    Alphacard Visa   28.0%</p>
<p>American Express 18.0%</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
